# library_books.dialogue — browsing the two library bookshelf stands.
# reached from Use on the shelves (unusables.dialogue imports this file).
# each row of a stand is one topic; each book opens one page via BookReader (data/library_books.gd).
# reading the heredity book sets dna_dates_found (the keypad follow-up stops pointing at Julian's lead).

~ left_stand
What do you want to look through?
- Scientific History
	=> left_history
- Genetics and Molecular Biology
	=> left_genetics
- Chemistry
	=> left_chemistry
- Statistics and Mathematics
	=> left_stats
- Nothing. Never mind. [Leave]
	=> END

~ left_history
Which book?
- Threads of Inheritance: A History of Heredity
	do BookReader.open("history_of_heredity")
	do Flags.set_level_flag("dna_dates_found", true)
	=> left_history
- Twisted Ladders: The Race for DNA
	do BookReader.open("race_for_the_helix")
	=> left_history
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> left_stand

~ left_genetics
Which book?
- On the Origin of Species (Darwin)
	do BookReader.open("darwin_origin")
	=> left_genetics
- The Bench Guide to Sequencing
	do BookReader.open("sequencing_handbook")
	=> left_genetics
- Safety Guidelines for Overworked Grad Students
	do BookReader.open("grad_safety_guidelines")
	=> left_genetics
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> left_stand

~ left_chemistry
Which book?
- Nothing Is Lost
	do BookReader.open("conservation_of_mass")
	=> left_chemistry
- Laboratory Safety, 9th Edition
	do BookReader.open("lab_safety")
	=> left_chemistry
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> left_stand

~ left_stats
Which book?
- The Trouble with P-Values
	do BookReader.open("p_values")
	=> left_stats
- Numbers for Nervous Biologists
	do BookReader.open("numbers_for_biologists")
	=> left_stats
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> left_stand

~ right_stand
What do you want to look through?
- Literature and Classics
	=> right_literature
- Philosophy
	=> right_philosophy
- Art and Architecture
	=> right_art
- University History
	=> right_history
- Nothing. Never mind. [Leave]
	=> END

~ right_literature
Which book?
- The Odyssey (Homer)
	do BookReader.open("homer_odyssey")
	=> right_literature
- Frankenstein (Mary Shelley)
	do BookReader.open("shelley_frankenstein")
	=> right_literature
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> right_stand

~ right_philosophy
Which book?
- The Republic (Plato)
	do BookReader.open("plato_republic")
	=> right_philosophy
- Utilitarianism (J. S. Mill)
	do BookReader.open("mill_utilitarianism")
	=> right_philosophy
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> right_stand

~ right_art
Which book?
- Rembrandt and the Light
	do BookReader.open("rembrandt_light")
	=> right_art
- Brick and Glass: The Buildings of Greendale
	do BookReader.open("campus_buildings")
	=> right_art
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> right_stand

~ right_history
Which book?
- A History of Greendale University
	do BookReader.open("greendale_history")
	=> right_history
- Greendale Yearbook
	do BookReader.open("yearbook")
	=> right_history
- Back to the shelves [Back]
	=> right_stand
